# _redirects — address rules Cloudflare Pages applies before serving a file.
# Why it exists: every family link looks like /register/<code> (one per event), but there is
# only ONE page, register.html. The line below serves that page for every such address while
# the address bar keeps the code (status 200 = "rewrite", not a visible redirect); the page
# then reads the code from the address.
# It points at /register (not /register.html) on purpose: Pages turns /register.html into
# /register by itself ("pretty URLs"), and pointing at the .html name can cause a redirect loop.
/register/*  /register  200

# The camp sign-up page works the same way (contract 0013 §4.1): every /camp/<code> address
# serves the ONE camp page, camp.html (Pages calls it /camp), and the page reads the code.
/camp/*  /camp  200

# The public Forms page (build plan §3): every family link looks like /f/<name> (e.g.
# /f/free-class-instagram), served by the one page forms.html in the same way. Pages serves
# forms.html at /forms by itself ("pretty URLs"), so both lines point at /forms. (/f alone, with
# no name, shows the page's "This form was not found".)
/f  /forms  200
/f/*  /forms  200

# The Star testing family links (/star/<code>) get their line from the BUILD, not from this file:
# vite.config.js (starRedirects) adds "/star/*  /star  200" to dist/_redirects while the Star build
# switch is on, and "/star" + "/star/*  /star-closed  200" (a plain "isn't open yet" page) while it is off.

# The public Black Belt testing registration page (CONTRACT-0016 §9.1): every family link looks
# like /black-belt/<code> (one per school per cycle), served by the one page black-belt.html in
# the same way. Pages serves black-belt.html at /black-belt by itself ("pretty URLs").
/black-belt/*  /black-belt  200
